    "title": "Parker Route history in Beaumont and Banning - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jeff Crider Record Gazette Contributor ,\n10 hours ago Metropolitan Water District considered more than 100 possible routes to transport Colorado River water across the Mojave Desert and into the Los Angeles Basin. “The search for the most practical and economical route would span seven years and involve one of the most comprehensive surveying efforts in history,” Joel Schwarz said in \"A Water Odyssey,” a 1991 book that documents the first half century of the Metropolitan Water District’s history. “It took hundreds of men to survey a vast expanse of desert, mountain and canyon country. In all, they charted more than 60,000 square miles of some of the loneliest and most desolate real estate in the United States.” Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
